      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. Noun suffixes"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        3.0,
        4.0,
        5.4,
        4.6
      ],
      "head": [
        "Suffix",
        "Forms",
        "Examples",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "-ción / -sión",
          "nouns from verbs (f.)",
          "comunicar: comunicación; decidir: decisión",
          "communication; decision"
        ],
        [
          "-miento",
          "nouns from verbs (m.)",
          "mover: movimiento; pensar: pensamiento",
          "movement; thought"
        ],
        [
          "-dad / -tad",
          "nouns from adjectives (f.)",
          "feliz: felicidad; libre: libertad",
          "happiness; freedom"
        ],
        [
          "-ez / -eza",
          "nouns from adjectives (f.)",
          "pobre: pobreza; tímido: timidez",
          "poverty; shyness"
        ],
        [
          "-ura",
          "nouns from adjectives (f.)",
          "alto: altura; abrir: apertura",
          "height; opening"
        ],
        [
          "-ismo / -ista",
          "doctrine / follower",
          "social: socialismo; arte: artista",
          "socialism; artist"
        ],
        [
          "-dor / -dora",
          "agent (person or machine)",
          "trabajar: trabajador; lavar: lavadora",
          "worker; washing machine"
        ],
        [
          "-ero / -era",
          "profession / container",
          "pan: panadero; ensalada: ensaladera",
          "baker; salad bowl"
        ],
        [
          "-ería",
          "shop / place",
          "libro: librería; pan: panadería",
          "bookshop; bakery"
        ],
        [
          "-aje / -anza",
          "result, action",
          "viajar: viaje; enseñar: enseñanza",
          "journey; teaching"
        ],
        [
          "-ncia / -nza",
          "state, quality",
          "paciente: paciencia; confiar: confianza",
          "patience; trust"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "title": "Gender follows the suffix",
      "text": "-ción, -sión, -dad, -tad, -ez, -eza, -ura, -ería, -ncia are <b>feminine</b>. -miento, -aje, -or and -ismo are <b>masculine</b>. Exceptions: <i>el avión, el corazón, la sartén</i> (no suffix rule)."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "3. Adjective and adverb suffixes"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        3.4,
        4.6,
        5.2,
        3.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Suffix",
        "Meaning",
        "Examples",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "-ble",
          "can be done",
          "comprar: comprable; creer: creíble",
          "buyable; credible"
        ],
        [
          "-oso / -osa",
          "full of",
          "peligro: peligroso; gracia: gracioso",
          "dangerous; funny"
        ],
        [
          "-ico / -al / -ar",
          "relating to",
          "teoría: teórico; ciudad: urbano",
          "theoretical; urban"
        ],
        [
          "-ivo / -ivo",
          "tending to",
          "decidir: decisivo; actuar: activo",
          "decisive; active"
        ],
        [
          "-ado / -ido",
          "participle adjective",
          "cansar: cansado; vivir: vivido",
          "tired; lived"
        ],
        [
          "-mente",
          "adverb of manner",
          "rápida: rápidamente; fácil: fácilmente",
          "quickly; easily"
        ],
        [
          "-ísimo",
          "very",
          "alto: altísimo",
          "very tall"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "-mente",
      "text": "Take the <b>feminine</b> adjective and add -mente: <i>lento: lentamente, claro: claramente, fácil: fácilmente</i>. The accent of the adjective is kept: <i>rápida: rápidamente</i>. With two adverbs in a row, only the last has -mente: <i>lenta y claramente</i>."
    },
